{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDeriv","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDeriv","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_classical","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L95-L107","doc":"When `q = 1`, `d_q` reduces to `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L85-L93","doc":"The q-deformed derivative `d_q` as a morphism: `q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ≫ d`.\nIn a preadditive ℝ-linear category, this is the explicit linear combination.\nThis is the categorical analogue of `qExtDeriv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_H","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L78-L83","doc":"The horizontal projection `π_H = id − π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Idempotency of the vertical projection: `π_V ∘ π_V = π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q_mul_qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q_mul_qinv","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L74-L74","doc":"`qinv` is the inverse of `q`. Replaces the former `q_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.qinv","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L72-L72","doc":"A two-sided inverse for `q`, carried as **data**.\n\nThe ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is a ring, not a field: it has no\n`Inv` instance, so `q⁻¹` cannot be *written* even though the\nindeterminate `q` is invertible in it. Carrying the inverse\nexplicitly, with its defining relation below, is the same move the\nQOU existence statement makes (`(q qinv : R) (hq : q * qinv = 1)`),\nand it is strictly stronger than the `q ≠ 0` it replaces —\nover a ring, invertible is not implied by nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.d_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.d_classical","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The classical differential `d : Ωᵏ(A) → Ωᵏ⁺¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L45-L76","doc":"**Categorical q-deformed exterior derivative**.\n\nOn a quantum observable universe with weight decomposition `π_H, π_V`\nand substrate parameter `q`, the q-deformed exterior derivative is\n`d_q = q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ∘ d`.  It acts as `q⁻¹ d` on horizontal\nforms and as `d` on vertical forms.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-q-ext-deriv}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-q-ext-deriv","label":"def:categorical-q-ext-deriv","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}